# OPTIONAL production dependencies — real Metasploit exploitation (opt-in).
#
# This lock is NOT installed by the default image or CI. It is only needed when
# an operator deliberately enables the human-gated real-exploit path
# (RECONX_REAL_EXPLOIT=true) against their own authorized msfrpcd. app.metasploit
# imports pymetasploit3 lazily and degrades to "unavailable" when it is absent,
# so the core safe-probe product runs without this file.
#
# Regenerate with:
#   pip-compile --generate-hashes --allow-unsafe \
#       --output-file=requirements-optional.txt requirements-optional.in
# Install (opt-in only):
#   pip install --require-hashes -r requirements-optional.txt
#
# RESIDUAL RISK (accepted, documented — NOT silently suppressed):
#   pymetasploit3==1.0.6 carries PYSEC-2026-500 with NO upstream fix available.
#   Because the package is confined to this opt-in file, the advisory does NOT
#   apply to the default deployment. Operators who install this file accept the
#   residual risk; it is mitigated by the fact that the exploit path is
#   human-gated, scope-checked, and only runs against operator-authorized hosts.
#   Re-evaluate when pymetasploit3 ships a fixed release.
pymetasploit3>=1.0.6
